<p>Switzerland said it will keep withholding payments for its order of five US-made Patriot air defence systems until Washington provides binding new delivery dates. Officials also said canceling the purchase remains on the table. The move reflects growing frustration after Bern learned last year that deliveries, originally set to begin in 2026 and finish in 2028, would be pushed back as the United States prioritized additional support for Ukraine. Swiss Defence Minister Martin Pfister said the government still assumes the systems may eventually arrive, but it does not know when and is reviewing several options, including cancellation. The dispute now goes beyond scheduling: Switzerland said last week that US authorities had drawn money from a Swiss Foreign Military Sales fund that Bern had frozen for the Patriot purchase, using liquidity intended for its F-35A fighter jet acquisition. Swiss officials said the step had been authorized, but warned it could put other Swiss projects at risk if the fund drops too low.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/iV4UEotRijA4utYOVh0BC9_-3y1tXrIA5-gG0oUJneUU7WvWrYVaqHHspDhfv-46_b_Y0U8CTNPTGmcjmmL7jD79MAuoXD55SA3MiwT6pnqz' alt='Swiss Federal Councillor Martin Pfister speaks during a press conference as he visits Swiss army troops in Bure, Switzerland, May 26, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>2022 purchase: Switzerland, which is not a NATO member, ordered the Patriot systems in 2022 as part of a broader push to strengthen national air defence.</li><li>Payment freeze: Bern first halted Patriot-related payments in autumn 2025 after the United States signaled delivery delays, and it has now said the freeze will stay in place until it gets firm dates and revised payment deadlines.</li><li>Fund pressure: The Swiss defence ministry warned that if liquidity in the shared Foreign Military Sales fund falls below a critical threshold, projects could be paused or abandoned, affecting not just Patriot but Switzerland’s broader US procurement portfolio.</li></ul><blockquote>Cancellation is always an option in the event of a delay. - Martin Pfister</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Swiss government: The government said it will keep withholding Patriot payments until the United States provides firm new delivery dates and payment deadlines. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/switzerland-says-cancelling-u-s-patriot-missile-system-order-an-option'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Martin Pfister: The defence minister said Switzerland still assumes the systems may be delivered, but is weighing several options because it does not know when they would arrive. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1987564/swiss-government-eyes-dropping-purchase-of-us-patriot-air-defence-system'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Urs Loher: The head of Switzerland’s armaments department said the US move to draw on the shared fund was authorized, even though Bern had frozen payments for the Patriot system. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1987564/swiss-government-eyes-dropping-purchase-of-us-patriot-air-defence-system'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/switzerland-says-cancelling-u-s-patriot-missile-system-order-an-option'>Switzerland says cancelling US Patriot missile system order an option</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/01/switzerland-eyes-dropping-purchase-of-us-patriot-air-defence-system-over-delivery-delays'>Switzerland eyes dropping purchase of US Patriot air defence system over delivery delays</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1987564/swiss-government-eyes-dropping-purchase-of-us-patriot-air-defence-system'>Swiss government eyes dropping purchase of US Patriot air defence system</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1s9pz56/switzerland_says_cancelling_us_patriot_missile/'>Switzerland says cancelling U.S. Patriot missile system order an option<